          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy a <strong class="text-white">dust extractor</strong> if you generate fine dust for hours at a time or work with silica-bearing materials — there, it is health equipment. Buy a <strong class="text-white">shop vac</strong> for everything else, because it handles debris, water and abuse that an extractor is not built for.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most home workshops, the right answer is a good shop vac plus <strong class="text-white">a cyclone separator, a collection bag and a fine dust cartridge</strong>. That combination closes most of the gap for a fraction of the money.
          </p>
